  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If the graphs of \\(2y+x+3=0\\) and \\(3y+ax+2=0\\) are to meet at right angles, the value of \\(a\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\pm\\dfrac23\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-\\dfrac23\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(-\\dfrac32\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(6\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(-6\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": "-6"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1961-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The two slopes are \\(-\\frac{1}{2}\\) and \\(-\\frac{a}{3}.\\) Perpendicularity requires \\[ \\left(-\\frac12\\right)\\left(-\\frac a3\\right)=-1, \\] so \\(a=-6.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Put both equations into slope-intercept form",
        "The product of the slopes of perpendicular nonvertical lines is \\(-1\\)"
      ],
